            "pages": {
              "end": 145,
              "start": 145
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to General Elizabeth B. Prelogar, the Supreme Court has long recognized that student\u2011body diversity is a compelling governmental interest that can justify limited consideration of race in admissions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "General Elizabeth B. Prelogar",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b15032ff7827-0006-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 147,
              "start": 147
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to General Elizabeth B. Prelogar, benefits of diversity include increased cross\u2011racial understanding and positive effects on cognitive development early in college."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b15032ff7827-0007-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 156,
              "start": 156
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, states that have banned race\u2011consideration in admissions have experienced sharp declines in enrollment of underrepresented minority students, especially Black students."
      }
